    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Travel Expense Policy"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Valid from [DATE_1] for all employees of [ORG_1]. Owner: Finance department, [PERSON_1]. This policy replaces the travel expense guideline of 2022 and was agreed with the works council on [DATE_2]."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "1. Purpose"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This policy sets out how business trips at [ORG_1] are approved, booked and settled. It aims to ensure that employees can travel safely and comfortably, that costs remain reasonable and that all expenses are documented in a way that meets the requirements of the tax authorities. The tax-free allowances mentioned in this policy are based on the current German income tax rules; if these rules change, Finance will update the amounts and inform all employees."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "2. Scope"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The policy applies to all employees, trainees and working students who travel on behalf of [ORG_1] in Germany or abroad. A business trip is any journey that an employee undertakes for work purposes away from their regular place of work and their home, for example customer visits, trade fairs, supplier audits, training courses or meetings at another site of the company. Journeys between home and the regular place of work are not business trips and are not reimbursed under this policy."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Travel by members of the management board and travel paid for by customers under a service contract may be subject to separate rules. In case of doubt, please contact Finance before you book."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "3. Approval of Business Trips"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Every business trip must be approved before any bookings are made. Please follow these steps:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Submit a travel request in the expense tool at least five working days before departure, stating the purpose, destination, dates and estimated costs."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Your manager approves or rejects the request within two working days. Trips abroad and trips with estimated costs above EUR 2,500 additionally require the approval of the head of department."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "For trips to countries outside the European Union, check the travel and safety information in the expense tool and contact HR if a visa or a vaccination is required."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Once the request is approved, book transport and accommodation through the travel agency portal, or, if this is not possible, directly with the provider."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "After the trip, submit your expense report within four weeks, attaching all receipts."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In urgent cases, such as a short-notice service call at a customer's site, the approval may be obtained by phone or email and entered in the tool afterwards. The reason for the urgency must be stated in the travel request."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "4. Means of Transport"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "When choosing a means of transport, consider the total cost, the travel time and the environmental impact. As a general rule, rail is preferred for trips within Germany and to neighbouring countries if the travel time does not exceed five hours."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Rail"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Rail journeys are booked in second class. First class may be booked for journeys of more than three hours or if the price difference is less than EUR 30, so that the travel time can be used for work. Employees who travel frequently by rail may apply for a rail discount card, which the company pays if the expected savings exceed the price of the card. Seat reservations are reimbursed."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Air"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Flights are only permitted if the destination cannot reasonably be reached by rail within five hours or if the flight is significantly cheaper overall. Domestic flights require the approval of the head of department. Flights are booked in economy class; for intercontinental flights with a flight time of more than eight hours, premium economy may be booked. Business class is only permitted with the approval of the management board. Checked baggage is reimbursed if it is necessary for the purpose of the business trip, for example to transport samples or measuring equipment."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Car"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pool cars are available at the main site and should be used for business trips by car whenever possible. They can be booked in the fleet management system. If no pool car is available, a rental car of the compact class may be booked through the travel agency portal. Employees who use their private car for a business trip with the approval of their manager receive a mileage allowance. Parking fees and tolls are reimbursed on presentation of receipts; fines for traffic or parking offences are never reimbursed."
          }
        ]
      },
