        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "5. Accommodation"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hotels are booked through the travel agency portal, which shows hotels with negotiated corporate rates. The following maximum rates per night including breakfast apply: EUR 130 in Germany, EUR 170 in [LOCATION_1] and [LOCATION_2] during trade fairs, and the rates listed in the portal for trips abroad. Higher rates must be justified, for example by a trade fair or a lack of alternatives near the customer's site. If breakfast is included in the hotel price, the meal allowance is reduced as described in section 6."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Employees who stay with friends or family during a business trip receive a flat rate of EUR 20 per night. Private stays before or after a business trip are not reimbursed and must be stated in the expense report."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "6. Meal Allowances"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "For business trips, employees receive a meal allowance to cover the additional costs of meals. The allowance depends on the duration of absence from home and the regular place of work. For trips abroad, the country-specific rates published by the Federal Ministry of Finance apply; they are stored in the expense tool."
          }
        ]
